    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "The Pan American Health Organization has revoked the measles elimination statuses of Bolivia, Mexico, and the United States.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-17:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "For the U.S., the organization cited continuous domestic transmission for over 12 months, amid more than 5,700 reported infections and multiple deaths in 2026.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-17:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Canada had lost its Measles Elimination Status in November 2025, after the virus had circulated for at least 12 months, and by the end of the outbreak in October 2026, over 6,400 cases had been recorded there.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386425034:0",
        "wiki:rev:1386425034:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "On the map, Bolivia is one of the three countries affected by the decision.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-17:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "The story was reported by AFP, via France 24 and Al Jazeera.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-17:12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:41Z",
      "text": "DW headlined the story, “US and Mexico lose measles-free status.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:dw:f59bc5b58da7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:47Z",
      "text": "France 24 framed it as “US, Mexico and Bolivia lose measles-free status as deaths mount.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:3ecebbb665bd"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:00:53Z",
      "text": "BBC News headlined it, “US loses measles elimination status after 26 years amid record case numbers.”",
      "cites": [
        "news:bbc:7e169f37829a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-17T00:01:02Z",
